insomniacUNDERSCORElemon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insomniacUNDERSCORElemon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T21:05:51Z","updated_at":"2025-06-08T20:18:33Z","body":"With _one_ of my models I'm seeing the opposite of this issue:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/825e4e4e-33a5-4b38-9401-a777988d1bf5)\n\nNot sure if there's anything I could do Blender-side to fix this.\n\nNote that the model on the left should be gray. The white level is reduced by higher roughness, can be reduced with low specular and low metallic but in both cases it's too bright if they have non-0 values (though metallic is much more important here, will still be too bright with 0 specular).\n\nFor models where this isn't an issue (see model on right) I need to increase roughness (much higher than compared to per-pixel) so the specular highlight can be seen at all times (note the rotation animation track, with low roughness the highlighted face flashes in and out in per-vertex).\n\nEDIT: Aside from roughness this can be prevented by setting specular mode to disabled, so might be a different issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comm